{"id":"effect-884f8810-d7fb-54a4-981e-c688dadd22a5","sessionId":"52c66c4e-33b0-9221-f436-2f4af6c4403d","turnId":"turn-10ae8a0133536bd00b52486b6e40931c","inputEntryId":"user-turn-10ae8a0133536bd00b52486b6e40931c-1","createdAt":1794282643469,"updatedAt":1794282643484,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a float value (via `round(value, 4)`), which gets stored in the `similar` list as `{\"slug\": ..., \"score\": float}`. DynamoDB does not accept Python float types — it requires `Decimal` for numeric values. The first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the related stories.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float\n\nThis ensures the score values are DynamoDB-compatible Decimal types, preventing the 500 error on subsequent publishes.\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a float value (via `round(value, 4)`), which gets stored in the `similar` list as `{\"slug\": ..., \"score\": float}`. DynamoDB does not accept Python float types — it requires `Decimal` for numeric values. The first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the related stories.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float\n\nThis ensures the score values are DynamoDB-compatible Decimal types, preventing the 500 error on subsequent publishes.\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","approvalType":"always","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-mKwego/ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a float value (via `round(value, 4)`), which gets stored in the `similar` list as `{\"slug\": ..., \"score\": float}`. DynamoDB does not accept Python float types — it requires `Decimal` for numeric values. The first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the related stories.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float\n\nThis ensures the score values are DynamoDB-compatible Decimal types, preventing the 500 error on subsequent publishes.\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"approvalSource":"bypass"}}
