{"id":"effect-7f5b5f73-d2be-5f54-9037-fc6a09ad4542","sessionId":"52c66c4e-33b0-9221-f436-2f4af6c4403d","turnId":"turn-10ae8a0133536bd00b52486b6e40931c","inputEntryId":"user-turn-10ae8a0133536bd00b52486b6e40931c-1","createdAt":1794282653252,"updatedAt":1794282653258,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading ANSWER.md","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","offset":null,"limit":2000}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","approvalType":"always","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"12 lines from ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-mKwego/ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function returns a float value (via `round(value, 4)`), which gets stored in the `similar` list as `{\"slug\": ..., \"score\": float}`. DynamoDB does not accept Python float types — it requires `Decimal` for numeric values. The first publish succeeds because there are no existing stories, so `related()` returns an empty list. The second publish fails because it tries to store float scores for the related stories.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float\n\nThis ensures the score values are DynamoDB-compatible Decimal types, preventing the 500 error on subsequent publishes.\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"requestedOffset":null,"requestedLimit":2000,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":false},"approvalSource":"bypass"}}
{"id":"assistant-9cb44515-3219-5131-bbdf-eb23ec0be50b","sessionId":"52c66c4e-33b0-9221-f436-2f4af6c4403d","turnId":"turn-10ae8a0133536bd00b52486b6e40931c","inputEntryId":"user-turn-10ae8a0133536bd00b52486b6e40931c-1","createdAt":1794282655851,"updatedAt":1794282655851,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The task is complete. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem identified:** The second publish was failing with a 500 error because the `similarity()` function returned a Python `float` value, which DynamoDB cannot serialize. DynamoDB requires `Decimal` types for numeric values.\n\n**Root cause:** When the first story was published, there were no existing stories, so `related()` returned an empty list. When the second story was published, `related()` computed similarity scores (floats) for existing stories, and DynamoDB rejected them with: `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\n**Fix applied:** Modified `src/app.py` to:\n1. Import `Decimal` from the `decimal` module\n2. Convert the float result from `round()` to a `Decimal` by wrapping it in `Decimal(str(round(...)))`\n\n**Verification:** \n- All existing tests pass\n- Multiple consecutive publishes now work correctly\n- The score values are now `Decimal` types, compatible with DynamoDB\n\nThe cause and fix are documented in `ANSWER.md`."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
